bility":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.08629771731580915,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013619897218919956,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.12528,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":83.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.96,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":96.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"NB Bancorp, Inc. focuses on operating as a bank holding company for Needham Bank that provides various banking products and services in the Greater Boston metropolitan area and surrounding communities in the United States. The company offers various deposits, including certificate of deposit, individual retirement, money market, savings, NOW, demand deposit, and interest-bearing and noninterest-bearing checking accounts; and commercial real estate and multifamily residential loans, one- to four-family residential real estate, mortgage warehouse loans, construction and land development, commercial and industrial, and consumer loans, as well as home equity loans and lines of credit. It also invests in securities consisting of U.S. treasury and federal agency securities, government-sponsored residential mortgage-backed securities, corporate bonds, SBA securities and municipal bonds. NB Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1892 and is based in Needham, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph P. Campanelli | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 69 | Compensation: $3.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 526 people. Revenue per employee of $406K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 21%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $109K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["NB Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $958M market cap on $214M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +12.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $57M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.21\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 8.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 50% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (96% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(NBBK) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/NBBK_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_110626125002_1793944202.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793944202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Contrasting Burke & Herbert Financial Services (NASDAQ:BHRB) and NB Bancorp (NASDAQ:NBBK)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/contrasting-burke-herbert-financial-services-nasdaqbhrb-and-nb-bancorp-nasdaqnbbk.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793441708.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NB Bancorp (NASDAQ:NBBK) Sets New 12-Month High \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/27/nb-bancorp-nasdaqnbbk-sets-new-12-month-high-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793109723.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NB Bancorp, Inc. (NBBK) To Go Ex-Dividend on October 29th","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/17/nb-bancorp-inc-nbbk-to-go-ex-dividend-on-october-29th.html","date":"2026-10-17","timestamp":1792248654.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"NB Bancorp GAAP EPS of $0.58 in-line, revenue of $76.5M misses by $0.8M (NASDAQ:NBBK)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4653645-nb-bancorp-gaap-eps-of-0_58-in-line-revenue-of-76_5m-misses-by-0_8m","date":"2026-10-15","timestamp":1792097126.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"NB Bancorp, Inc. (NBBK) Q3 Earnings Beat Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3008891/nb-bancorp-inc-nbbk-q3-earnings-beat-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3008891","date":"2026-10-15","timestamp":1792096502.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"NB Bancorp declares $0.07 dividend (NASDAQ:NBBK)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4653624-nb-bancorp-declares-0_07-dividend","date":"2026-10-15","timestamp":1792095971.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"NB Bancorp Announces $100M 7.50% Fixed-to-Float